{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ad7330b2-9d94-4b18-9534-ab76204119f3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-90384708cb11890f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-np2t8pyv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E002.md","content":"# Llama Stack API Stability Guarantee: Versioned APIs, Deprecation Policy, Tested Upgrade Path\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic puts a stability guarantee on Llama Stack's published API surface so\nenterprise customers can build production GenAI applications against it. It\ndelivers versioned APIs, a published deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade\npath from the last two Tech Preview releases, plus remediation of the\nAPI-stability and upgrade-path gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment.\n\n## Description of Dependencies\n\nThis epic's scope is gated by the GA-readiness assessment: the assessment\nproduces the definitive GA scope, and its API-stability and upgrade-path\nfindings determine which surfaces must be stabilized and how much hardening\nwork is in scope. If the assessment surfaces gaps beyond the current scope\nestimate, this epic's scope is rewritten to absorb them.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Introduce API versioning on the published Llama Stack API surface (the\n  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the LlamaStackDistribution CRD surface).\n- Define and publish a deprecation policy covering how API changes are\n  versioned, announced, and retired.\n- Build and test an upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases to\n  the GA release, including migration of existing LlamaStackDistribution\n  custom resources.\n- Remediate the API-stability and upgrade-path gaps inventoried by the\n  GA-readiness assessment that are dispositioned into GA scope.\n- Ensure the component's existing Konflux build pipeline remains green for\n  all changes in this epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Published APIs carry explicit version identifiers, and the versioning scheme\n  is documented.\n- A deprecation policy is published describing versioning, notice periods,\n  and removal rules for API changes.\n- An automated or repeatable upgrade test demonstrates successful upgrade from\n  each of the last two Tech Preview releases to the GA release, including\n  preservation of existing distribution custom resources.\n- Every API-stability and upgrade-path gap from the GA-readiness assessment\n  that was dispositioned into GA scope is remediated or explicitly accepted\n  with a documented limitation.\n- The Konflux build pipeline for the Llama Stack component is green with the\n  changes in this epic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned\n  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n  releases.\n- HLR-1 (P0, partial): remediation of the assessment-inventoried\n  API-stability, upgrade-path, error-handling, and scale-limit gaps\n  dispositioned into GA scope on the API surface.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31489,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aacd8cd5f20921ac","agent_id":"aea554450e8b70b1d","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"0fc15165-f3e6-4580-93ce-dc9a55675939","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:07:14.564Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
