{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab8287de4b3b0d4c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9014: Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: RHAISTRAT-9014 (Critical priority, Refinement Done).\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold: the strategy spans three affected components (Llama Stack,\n17\tTrustyAI, Dashboard) plus a documentation uplift stream, owned by three distinct\n18\tteams — architecturally distinct sub-systems warranting separate PR review\n19\tcycles. Not docs-only: substantive code and integration work is required.\n20\tProceeded with full DAG decomposition.\n21\t\n22\t## Strategy Structure Parse\n23\t\n24\tSections present: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements (HLR-1..HLR-6),\n25\tAffected Components (Llama Stack, TrustyAI, Dashboard), Out of Scope, Open\n26\tQuestions.\n27\t\n28\tSections missing (health warnings, proceeded with available information):\n29\tImpacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then),\n30\tNon-Functional Requirements. Owner teams were derived from the architecture\n31\tcontext files (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`). No\n32\tStaff Engineer Input section exists in the strategy.\n33\t\n34\t## Component Graph\n35\t\n36\tAll three affected components are in the platform (architecture context files\n37\texist for each), so no onboarding chain is required:\n38\t\n39\t- **Llama Stack** — Active. Tech Preview today (corroborated by\n40\t  `architecture/rhoai-3.0/llama-stack.md`); GA graduation work is the core of\n41\t  the strategy. Owner: RHOAI GenAI. Konflux onboarded.\n42\t- **TrustyAI** — Active. HLR-4 requires the guardrails integration to become a\n43\t  supported, documented integration rather than an experimental flag. Owner:\n44\t  TrustyAI team.\n45\t- **Dashboard** — Active. HLR-5 requires Llama Stack management enabled by\n46\t  default for entitled clusters (remove the TP opt-in gate). Owner: RHOAI\n47\t  Dashboard.\n48\t- **Documentation** — appears via HLR-6 (GA-standard docs uplift with TP\n49\t  migration notes); substantive content authoring, handled as a separate\n50\t  `docs-authoring` epic assigned to the Llama Stack owning team (RHOAI GenAI),\n51\t  since no Impacted Teams table exists to assign a docs team.\n52\t\n53\tComponent name mapping note: all epic `component` values are copied verbatim\n54\tfrom `.context/rhai-components.txt` (`Llama Stack`, `TrustyAI`, `Dashboard`,\n55\t`Documentation`). No non-obvious mappings were needed.\n56\t\n57\t## Step 0/1 Analysis: The Central Unknown\n58\t\n59\tThe strategy's defining characteristic (Problem Statement + Open Question 1) is\n60\tthat the GA gap inventory is unknown: TP feedback is scattered across support\n61\ttickets and no systematic GA-readiness assessment has been done. HLR-1 makes\n62\tthat assessment a P0 deliverable that \"produc[es] the definitive GA scope\".\n63\tPer the Step 3 decision rule, this answer changes what downstream epics do (the\n64\tsize and content of the stability and hardening work), so HLR-1 becomes an\n65\tInvestigation epic gating the scope-defining implementations. The outcome space\n66\tis unbounded (an unknown inventory of gaps), so no conditional branches are\n67\temitted — the gate is recorded via `gated_by` / `gate_failure_impact` on the\n68\tdownstream epics.\n69\t\n70\t## Epic List\n71\t\n72\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n73\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n74\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 | GA-readiness assessment producing the definitive GA scope | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n75\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 | Llama Stack API stability guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n76\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 | Llama Stack production support posture: SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n77\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 | TrustyAI guardrails as a supported, documented Llama Stack integration | Implementation | TrustyAI | P1 |\n78\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 | Dashboard: enable Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n79\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 | Llama Stack GA documentation uplift with TP migration notes | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n80\t\n81\tE006 priority note: per the docs-authoring priority exception, E006's priority\n82\tis derived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0, not from\n83\tHLR-6's P2 label, and it does not push priority upstream onto the\n84\timplementations it depends on.\n85\t\n86\t## Dependency DAG\n87\t\n88\t```mermaid\n89\tgraph TD\n90\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 GA-readiness assessment] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 API stability]\n91\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 Support posture]\n92\t    E002 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 TrustyAI supported integration]\n93\t    E002 --> E006[RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 GA docs uplift]\n94\t    E003 --> E006\n95\t    E004 --> E006\n96\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 Dashboard default enablement] --> E006\n97\t```\n98\t\n99\tCritical path: E001 → E002 → E004 → E006 (4 epics).\n100\t\n101\t## DAG Justification\n102\t\n103\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n104\t|------|------|-----------|\n105\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The GA scope defined by the assessment determines the size and content of the API stability and hardening work; Open Question 1 states the work size \"is an estimate\" until it lands. True gate: `rewrite` — assessment findings (e.g. additional unstable API surfaces, upgrade-path gaps) change what E002 must do. |\n106\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The assessment's scale-limit and error-handling findings feed the supported configuration matrix and SLO targets; the GA bar the posture must meet is defined by the assessment. True gate: `rewrite`. |\n107\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer serial) | The TrustyAI guardrails integration builds against the Llama Stack API surface; a supported integration must target the published, versioned, stability-guaranteed API and deprecation policy rather than the TP surface it replaces. |\n108\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | GA documentation must describe the versioned API surface, deprecation policy, and upgrade path that E002 delivers. |\n109\t| E003 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | GA documentation must reflect the published SLO targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. |\n110\t| E004 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | The TrustyAI guardrails integration must be documented as supported; docs describe what was built. |\n111\t| E005 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring last) | Documentation must cover default enablement for entitled clusters (removal of the TP opt-in gate). |\n112\t\n113\tDeliberately absent edges:\n114\t\n115\t- **E001/E002/E003 → E005**: the Dashboard default-enablement change is an\n116\t  independent code change in a different repo (feature-flag default in\n117\t  `OdhDashboardConfig`); the GA-milestone timing of flipping the default is a\n118\t  release-coordination point, not an artifact dependency (Rule 14/15). Kept\n119\t  parallel.\n120\t- **E001 → E004**: HLR-4 is a self-defined deliverable (promote the existing\n121\t  experimental TrustyAI integration to supported); its scope does not change\n122\t  based on the Llama Stack gap inventory. Not gated by the investigation.\n123\t- **E003 ∥ E002**: same team and component, but distinct work-product\n124\t  surfaces (code/API hardening vs. support-process/policy artifacts); both are\n125\t  gated by E001 and can proceed in parallel once the GA scope lands. No\n126\t  serializing edge (Rule 15).\n127\t\n128\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n129\t\n130\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n131\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n132\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 | GA-readiness assessment; the Investigation itself is the deliverable. Remediation items it surfaces are absorbed into E002/E003 scope via their `gate_failure_impact` (add/rewrite). |\n133\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 | Versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases. |\n134\t| HLR-3 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 | SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix. |\n135\t| HLR-4 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 | TrustyAI guardrails as supported, documented integration. |\n136\t| HLR-5 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 | Dashboard default enablement for entitled clusters. |\n137\t| HLR-6 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 | (bundled into a single docs-authoring epic at strategy-level Critical priority per the docs-authoring priority exception) — GA docs uplift and TP migration notes are one documentation work stream over one docs surface; not separately schedulable from the rest of the docs uplift. |\n138\t\n139\tAll six HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n140\t\n141\t## Tiered Delivery\n142\t\n143\tNot applicable. There is no external upstream dependency with uncertain\n144\ttiming: all work is in platform-owned midstream repos, and the sole open\n145\tquestion (the GA scope) is resolved by an internal Investigation, not an\n146\texternal party. HLR-4/HLR-5 (P1) naturally deliver partial value ahead of the\n147\tfull GA bar and are not blocked by the P0 chain.\n148\t\n149\t## Health Warnings\n150\t\n151\t- **Missing strategy sections**: no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table,\n152\t  Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, or NFRs. Teams were derived from\n153\t  architecture context; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR text.\n154\t  Human verification of team assignments recommended.\n155\t- **Unbounded gate**: the E001 assessment outcome is unbounded (unknown gap\n156\t  inventory). If it surfaces substantial remediation beyond E002/E003 scope\n157\t  (e.g. large-scale error-handling or scale-limit rework), the decomposition\n158\t  should be revisited and new implementation epics spawned — recorded as\n159\t  `gate_failure_impact.action=add_remediation` semantics on the gated epics.\n160\t- **Priority inversion watch**: E006 carries P0 (strategy-level Critical via\n161\t  the docs-authoring exception) even though its underlying HLR-6 is P2. This\n162\t  is per-spec, not an error, but reviewers should not read it as docs work\n163\t  blocking the GA bar.\n164\t- **Coordination (not dependency)**: E005's flag flip should land at the GA\n165\t  release boundary; this is release-train coordination, deliberately not a DAG\n166\t  edge.\n167\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be5e4b54ab7e4a92","agent_id":"a67c33ecfdcb2bba0","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"cdd92151-4074-4d93-a876-d329c63f116e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:44.275Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab8287de4b3b0d4c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
