{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-849bc43a1623f748","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment producing the definitive GA scope\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-Readiness Assessment Producing the Definitive GA Scope\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: the full inventory of gaps\n30\tbetween Llama Stack's current Tech Preview quality and the General\n31\tAvailability bar. It systematically consolidates TP feedback scattered across\n32\tsupport tickets, architecture context, and the platform's GA criteria, and\n33\tproduces the definitive GA scope that all downstream stability, hardening, and\n34\tsupport-posture work is planned against.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Collect and triage Tech Preview feedback from support tickets, issue\n39\t  trackers, and known-issues records for the Llama Stack component.\n40\t- Assess current state against the GA bar in the four dimensions named by the\n41\t  strategy: API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling.\n42\t- Produce a GA-readiness report: a gap inventory with severity, affected\n43\t  surfaces, and recommended disposition for each gap.\n44\t- Produce the definitive GA scope document: which gaps are in scope for GA,\n45\t  deferred, or accepted with documented limitations.\n46\t- Flag any gap whose remediation would require work beyond the stability and\n47\t  support-posture streams (e.g. substantial error-handling or scale-limit\n48\t  rework) so the epic plan can be revisited.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A GA-readiness report exists that inventories gaps across API stability,\n53\t  upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling, with each gap traceable to\n54\t  its feedback source.\n55\t- Every gap in the inventory has a disposition: in GA scope, deferred, or\n56\t  accepted-with-limitation.\n57\t- The definitive GA scope document is published and agreed with stakeholders,\n58\t  such that downstream stability and support-posture work can be sized against\n59\t  it rather than estimated.\n60\t- Feedback sources consulted are listed in the report, covering the support\n61\t  ticket record of the Tech Preview period.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP\n66\t  quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error\n67\t  handling), producing the definitive GA scope — this epic is that assessment.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be5e4b54ab7e4a92","agent_id":"a67c33ecfdcb2bba0","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"09da0049-c1de-4dc3-8d20-2c5db3c87d95","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:46.334Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-849bc43a1623f748","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
