he assessment's scale-limit findings).\n50\t- Define and document a backport policy: which releases receive fixes, for how\n51\t  long, and how backports are delivered.\n52\t- Define and publish a supported configuration matrix: the provider plugins,\n53\t  inference providers, vector/RAG providers, and deployment topologies that\n54\t  are supported and tested at GA.\n55\t- Capture support-commitment content in the appropriate product\n56\t  documentation/policy locations, aligned with the platform's existing\n57\t  support-posture conventions for GA components.\n58\t- Fold in any support-posture gaps the GA-readiness assessment dispositions\n59\t  into GA scope.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Documented SLO targets exist and are published for the GA release.\n64\t- A backport policy is published stating supported release windows and\n65\t  backport delivery mechanics.\n66\t- A supported configuration matrix is published listing the tested, supported\n67\t  provider and deployment combinations, with unsupported combinations\n68\t  explicitly marked.\n69\t- Every support-posture gap from the GA-readiness assessment dispositioned\n70\t  into GA scope is addressed or explicitly accepted with a documented\n71\t  limitation.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-3 (P0): Production support posture is in place: documented SLO targets,\n76\t  backport policy, and supported configuration matrix.\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0, partial): scale-limit and error-handling findings from the\n78\t  assessment feed the SLO targets and configuration matrix.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be5e4b54ab7e4a92","agent_id":"a67c33ecfdcb2bba0","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"193770b5-5f61-4a4d-8a76-94dde0fd999d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:52.796Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e6c06bfd6a793eb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_descr