{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be783afcba16650","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n3\ttitle: 'Dashboard: enable Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard: Enable Llama Stack Management by Default for Entitled Clusters\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic removes the Tech Preview opt-in gate for Llama Stack management in\n34\tthe Dashboard, so that Llama Stack management is enabled by default for\n35\tentitled clusters at GA. The Dashboard owns the feature-flag default and the\n36\tuser-facing management experience.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Change the Llama Stack management feature flag from an opt-in (Tech Preview\n41\t  gate) to enabled-by-default for entitled clusters, following the Dashboard's\n42\t  existing per-component feature-flag and defaults mechanism.\n43\t- Verify the Llama Stack management experience (navigation section, resource\n44\t  views, and any creation/status surfaces the Dashboard already ships for\n45\t  Llama Stack) works correctly when enabled by default.\n46\t- Handle entitlement gating: default-on applies only to entitled clusters;\n47\t  non-entitled clusters must not see Llama Stack management.\n48\t- Update Dashboard feature-flag documentation/defaults references that fall\n49\t  out of this change.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- On an entitled cluster with default configuration (no opt-in set), Llama\n54\t  Stack management is available in the Dashboard with no manual feature-flag\n55\t  change.\n56\t- On a non-entitled cluster, Llama Stack management remains hidden.\n57\t- Existing opt-in configurations continue to work (no regression for clusters\n58\t  that explicitly enabled the feature during Tech Preview).\n59\t- The Dashboard's automated test suite covers the default-on entitlement\n60\t  behavior and passes.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-5 (P1): The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n65\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be5e4b54ab7e4a92","agent_id":"a67c33ecfdcb2bba0","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"6d341356-0fa1-4497-9b1c-9f8b6fb4c84f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:55.780Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be783afcba16650","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
