127\t`gated_by`.\n128\t\n129\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n130\tSignal fields are type-correct (E001 carries `investigation_signals` with all\n131\t5 signals; E002–E006 carry the 9-signal `ai_signals`); all six ai-signals\n132\trationale files exist and their values match the frontmatter.\n133\t`architecture_claims: 1` is well calibrated — every epic that rests on the\n134\tstrategy's Tech-Premise premise cites the matching\n135\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/` file, and the claims\n136\tcheck out against those files (Llama Stack Tech Preview, CRD + OpenAI-compatible\n137\tAPIs; TrustyAI GA with guardrails; Dashboard feature flags via\n138\tOdhDashboardConfig). Investigation signal values for E001 are consistent with\n139\tthe strategy (question_specificity +1 for the four named dimensions;\n140\thuman_judgment_required -1 for the stakeholder scoping decision).\n141\t\n142\tMinor (arguable value): E004 scores `human_process_gates: 0` on the grounds\n143\tthat declaring the integration \"supported\" is folded into the GA process, while\n144\tE003 scores `-1` because publishing SLO/backport commitments requires\n145\tleadership approval. Listing the guardrails integration as a supported\n146\tconfiguration (E004's own AC) is the same class of support-posture commitment\n147\tE003 flags — the calibration between the two epics is inconsistent, and\n148\t`human_process_gates: -1` for E004 would be equally defensible.\n149\t\n150\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n151\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs are\n152\tpresent where applicable: E006 has the technical-review-against-implementation\n153\tAC; E002 and E004 carry the Konflux build-pipeline-green AC for their\n154\tKonflux-onboarded components; E002's upgrade-path AC (from each of the last two\n155\tTP releases, preserving existing custom resources) covers the migration\n156\trequirement. No externally-controlled precondition is misfiled 