{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7394b7940ac9c91","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Llama Stack API stability guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested\n4\t  upgrade path'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n6\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n7\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment inventories stability or upgrade-path\n16\t    gaps beyond the estimated scope, rewrite this epic's scope to absorb the additional\n17\t    hardening; if remediation exceeds stability work entirely, spawn additional implementation\n18\t    epics from the assessment findings.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Llama Stack API Stability Guarantee: Versioned APIs, Deprecation Policy, Tested Upgrade Path\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic puts a stability guarantee on Llama Stack's published API surface so\n41\tenterprise customers can build production GenAI applications against it. It\n42\tdelivers versioned APIs, a published deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade\n43\tpath from the last two Tech Preview releases, plus remediation of the\n44\tAPI-stability and upgrade-path gaps that the GA-readiness assessment\n45\tidentifies and dispositions into GA scope. The epic is gated by the\n46\tGA-readiness assessment: its findings determine which surfaces must be\n47\tstabilized and how much hardening work is in scope.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Introduce API versioning on the published Llama Stack API surface (the\n52\t  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the LlamaStackDistribution CRD surface).\n53\t- Define and publish a deprecation policy covering how API changes are\n54\t  versioned, announced, and retired.\n55\t- Build and test an upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases to\n56\t  the GA release, including migration of existing LlamaStackDistribution\n57\t  custom resources.\n58\t- Remediate the API-stability and upgrade-path gaps inventoried by the\n59\t  GA-readiness assessment that are dispositioned into GA scope.\n60\t- Ensure the component's existing Konflux build pipeline remains green for\n61\t  all changes in this epic.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Published APIs carry explicit version identifiers, and the versioning scheme\n66\t  is documented.\n67\t- A deprecation policy is published describing versioning, notice periods,\n68\t  and removal rules for API changes.\n69\t- An automated or repeatable upgrade test demonstrates successful upgrade from\n70\t  each of the last two Tech Preview releases to the GA release, including\n71\t  preservation of existing distribution custom resources.\n72\t- Every API-stability and upgrade-path gap from the GA-readiness assessment\n73\t  that was dispositioned into GA scope is remediated or explicitly accepted\n74\t  with a documented limitation.\n75\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the Llama Stack component is green with the\n76\t  changes in this epic.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-2 (P0): Published API surface carries a stability guarantee: versioned\n81\t  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n82\t  releases.\n83\t- HLR-1 (P0, partial): remediation of the assessment-inventoried\n84\t  API-stability and upgrade-path gaps dispositioned into GA scope on the\n85\t  API surface. Error-handling a