orted quality: error handling, failure\n51\t  modes, and configuration validation appropriate for a supported\n52\t  integration.\n53\t- Document the integration: supported deployment topology, configuration\n54\t  steps, and support boundaries between the TrustyAI and Llama Stack\n55\t  components. This epic authors the technical content for the integration;\n56\t  uplifting that content into the published GA documentation set at GA\n57\t  standard is owned separately by the documentation uplift work, which\n58\t  consumes this content as an input.\n59\t- Ensure the TrustyAI component's existing Konflux build pipeline remains\n60\t  green for changes in this epic.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Enabling TrustyAI guardrails on a GA Llama Stack distribution no longer\n65\t  requires an experimental flag, and the integration is listed as a supported\n66\t  configuration.\n67\t- The integration is validated against the versioned GA API surface, including\n68\t  behavior when the API signals deprecation.\n69\t- Documentation exists describing how to deploy, configure, and troubleshoot\n70\t  the guardrails integration, including the support boundary between the two\n71\t  components.\n72\t- The Konflux build pipeline for the TrustyAI component is green with the\n73\t  changes in this epic.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-4 (P1): Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n78\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95938061ebde5a25","agent_id":"a8015b283169ec80c","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"181b52d6-f8aa-4168-be03-4d68609d602f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:16:16.381Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-87ade7e3c57c3071","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014"}
