  customer-facing documentation.\n55\t- The TrustyAI guardrails integration documented as a supported configuration,\n56\t  including its support boundary. The TrustyAI team authors this technical\n57\t  content (deployment topology, configuration, troubleshooting) as part of the\n58\t  integration work; this epic's ownership is uplifting that content into the\n59\t  published GA documentation set at GA standard.\n60\t- Dashboard default enablement for entitled clusters reflected in\n61\t  documentation (removal of the TP opt-in instructions).\n62\t- Removal or correction of Tech Preview caveats and disclaimers that no\n63\t  longer apply at GA.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- Documentation covering installation, configuration, the versioned API\n68\t  surface, deprecation policy, and upgrade path is published at GA standard.\n69\t- Migration notes exist for each of the last two Tech Preview releases and\n70\t  are technically accurate against the tested upgrade path.\n71\t- All GA-scope deliverables (support posture, supported TrustyAI guardrails\n72\t  integration, Dashboard default enablement) are reflected in published\n73\t  documentation.\n74\t- No Tech Preview caveats or experimental-flag instructions remain in the\n75\t  Llama Stack documentation set.\n76\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation by\n77\t  someone with knowledge of the delivered GA scope.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- HLR-6 (P2): Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including migration\n82\t  notes from TP.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95938061ebde5a25","agent_id":"a8015b283169ec80c","session_id":"39ecee98-99e4-452a-b2b9-dea59d7dddfe","uuid":"a84b2cfb-115d-4617-9f47-9231876046a0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:16:17.889Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-973b095d1beb833b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description"